Z||000000||GT/SE WannaBee||04-17-2001||08:37 AM||||Does the interior of the fiero get quite warm because of the relative closeness of the motor to the seats?  Is air conditioning a must?||||reg||1
Z||000001||ChadMan||04-17-2001||08:47 AM||||Heat from the engine never seems to enter the interior...a Fiero with no A/C is no hotter than any other car without A/C.  I have an 88 Coupe with a sunroof, but no A/C, and the only time I miss the A/C is when it's humid and 85 or warmer (around 30 days/year in Columbus).<P>That said, I can't see myself buying another one without A/C, because those 30 days are miserable!||||reg||14
Z||000002||Raydar||04-17-2001||07:35 PM||||I'd second that. Fieros don't seem to get too hot inside, due to engine heat.<BR>Having said that... I live in Atlanta. AC will be a requirement in about four days.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 T-top Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
